## [upstream] min: fix the parabolic-step test in the Brent minimiser

Commit: c27559ec6

`brent_iterate()` takes the parabolic step `p/q` only when the trial point
`u = z + p/q` lies inside the bracket.  With `q` made positive that is
`-q*w_lower < p < q*w_upper`, but the code tested `p < q*w_lower`, which
admits trial points below `x_left` and rejects many valid parabolic steps,
forcing golden-section steps.  A transcription error from Brent's Algol 60;
netlib `fmin`, Numerical Recipes, Forsythe et al. and Boost all have the
corrected form.

Files: `min/brent.c`, plus a regression test in `min/test.c`/`min/test_funcs.c`.

See Savannah bug #43496.


## [upstream] monte: avoid inf weight in VEGAS when the box variance is subnormal

Commit: e3cab2d02

`gsl_monte_vegas_integrate()` computed `wgt = 1/var` whenever `var > 0`.
A tiny but non-zero subnormal `var` makes `1/var` overflow to `+Inf`, which
propagates into `wtd_int_sum` and makes the result (and `chisq`) `NaN`.
Any `var` for which `1/var` is not finite is now treated as zero.

Files: `monte/vegas.c`, plus a regression test in `monte/test.c`.

See Savannah bug #44612.


## [upstream] roots: initialise Newton and Steffenson with the combined fdf call

Commit: 4eac6584f

Both fdfsolvers initialised with separate `GSL_FN_FDF_EVAL_F` and
`GSL_FN_FDF_EVAL_DF` calls although their iterate step already uses the
combined `GSL_FN_FDF_EVAL_F_DF`.  A user function that computes value and
derivative together is now called once at setup instead of twice, and the
initialisation path matches the iteration path.

Files: `roots/newton.c`, `roots/steffenson.c`, plus a counting test in
`roots/test.c`.

See Savannah bug #49465.


## [upstream] specfunc: improve the accuracy of lambert_W0 for small arguments

Commit: fb2b4e4cd

`gsl_sf_lambert_W0_e(x)` always used the Halley iteration, whose `w -= t`
step cancels catastrophically for `x` near zero; the relative error grew as
`x` decreased and below about `1e-50` the result collapsed to zero.  For
`|x| < 1e-3 * GSL_DBL_EPSILON` it now returns `x`, and for `|x| < 1e-5` it
evaluates the Taylor series (Fukushima 2013).  The relative error is now of
order machine epsilon across the range.

Files: `specfunc/lambert.c`, plus tests in `specfunc/test_sf.c`.

See Savannah bug #60741.


## [upstream] const: update the physical constants to CODATA 2022

Commit: db695c8f2

The recommended values dated from around 2000.  The measured constants are
updated to CODATA 2022 and the SI-exact ones (c, h, e, k, N_A) are given
exactly.  The cgs and cgsm headers now define the physical constants in
terms of their mks counterparts so the four unit systems cannot drift apart,
and derivative relations are used where they apply (hbar = h/2 pi).  Add the
radiation density constant (4 sigma / c) and the WGS-84 / IUGG Earth radii
(R1 = (2a+b)/3).  Tests for the identities and pinned CODATA 2022 values are
added to `const/test.c`.

Note: this changes the numerical values of the affected constants.

Files: `const/gsl_const_{mksa,mks,cgs,cgsm,num}.h`, `const/test.c`,
`const/calc-units-update.el`, `const/const.el`, `const/TODO`.

See Savannah bug #60635.


