## [upstream] cdf: bracketed solver for the beta inverse

Commit: 51a63cbd5

gsl_cdf_beta_Pinv and _Qinv returned NaN for large a and b at any tail
probability away from one half.  The routine bisected to an absolute
tolerance Ptol = 0.01 in P and then ran an unsafeguarded Newton
iteration.  For a = 8000, b = 2000 the small-x starting approximation
already satisfies |Px - P| < 0.01 while being nowhere near the root, so
bisect returned it on the first pass; Newton then stepped in the wrong
direction and the final residual test raised "inverse failed to
converge".  Two further defects shared the root cause: for a << 1 the
quantile can lie hundreds of decades below the mean, which a bisection
on x cannot reach within the 64-step budget, and Qinv formed the upper
tail as 1 - Pinv(Q, b, a), losing every digit by cancellation when the
result is small.

Measured on the built DLL before the change: all ten cases in the
report (a = 8000, b = 2000; a = 630, b = 9370; a = 5000, b = 5000 at
P = 0.005, 0.995, 5e-5, 0.99995) returned NaN.

The solver now works on t = logit(x).  In both the lower-tail
(F = P(x) - target) and upper-tail (F = target - Q(x)) cases F is
monotone increasing in t, so [log(DBL_MIN), -log(DBL_MIN)] is always a
bracket.  A Newton step from the density is taken when it stays inside
the bracket and changes x, otherwise the bracket is halved; convergence
is accepted when the bracket closes, when the Newton step is below the
resolution of t, or when x can no longer change.  A root below
GSL_DBL_MIN returns zero, matching the gamma inverse.  Both entry
points now invert whichever tail is no larger than one half and
evaluate that tail directly, so Qinv no longer subtracts from one.

Verification.  References are scipy 1.15 `betaincinv` / `betainccinv`
at double precision, agreeing with the Boost values quoted in the
report.  All ten reported cases agree to about 4e-14 relative.  A
random grid of 73085 Pinv and 99658 Qinv points with a, b in
[1e-4, 1e4] and tail probability from 1e-12 to 1/2 has no failures and
a worst relative error of 7.4e-11, inside the TEST_TOL6 of 2.3e-10.
gsl_cdf_fdist_Pinv/Qinv delegate to this routine and inherit the fix;
two large-nu fdist vectors are added.

The regression vectors are the ten report cases for both Pinv and Qinv
plus the two fdist vectors, in `cdf/test.c`.  Negative control: with
`cdf/betainv.c` reverted, `cdf_test` aborts at the first new vector
with "inverse failed to converge" (exit 0xc0000409), and with the
error handler disabled all ten reported cases return NaN.  Full suite
56/56.

Files: `cdf/betainv.c`, `cdf/test.c`.

Savannah bug #45924.


## [upstream] statistics: reject empty data sets in the mean and variance family

Commit: 68fc3c752

gsl_stats_mean accumulated with the recurrence
mean += (x_i - mean)/(i+1), which leaves the accumulator at zero when
size is zero, so an empty data set returned 0.0 rather than the
undefined value its documented definition (1/N) sum x_i gives.  R and
numpy return NaN.  gsl_stats_variance and gsl_stats_sd inherited the
zero through variance_m, and their _m and fixed-mean variants returned
zero too: the empty loop produced zero and the 1/(N-1) or 1/N factor
could not correct it.

Measured with the built DLL: mean, variance and sd of a zero-length
array all returned 0.0.

gsl_stats_mean and the shared compute_variance helper - reached by
variance_m, sd_m, variance_with_fixed_mean and sd_with_fixed_mean, and
so by variance and sd - now raise GSL_EBADLEN for size zero.  With the
error handler disabled they return NaN.  gsl_stats_tss is deliberately
left alone: the total sum of squares of an empty set is genuinely
zero.

The behaviour is recorded in the mean/variance/sd section of both
manuals.

The empty-array checks in `statistics/test_float_source.c` and
`statistics/test_int_source.c` set the error handler off and assert NaN
for the double, float, long double and all eight integer types.
Negative control: with the two guards reverted `statistics_test`
reports 99 failures, all new ("... empty"); with them applied the
module is clean and the full suite is 56/56.

Files: `statistics/mean_source.c`, `statistics/variance_source.c`,
`statistics/mean.c`, `statistics/variance.c`, `statistics/test.c`,
`statistics/test_float_source.c`, `statistics/test_int_source.c`,
`doc/statistics.rst`, `doc_texinfo/statistics.texi`.

Savannah bug #67058.


